<given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular markers for failure of sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine and chlorproguanil-dapsone treatment of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum </italic>malaria</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>380</fpage><lpage>388</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11807721</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/338566</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kyabayinze</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cattamanchi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamya</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenthal</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorsey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validation of a simplified method for using molecular markers to predict sulfadoxine-pyrimethamine treatment failure in African children with falciparum malaria</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>247</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14628939</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wellems</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Plowe</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chloroquine-resistant malaria</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>184</volume><fpage>770</fpage><lpage>776</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11517439</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/322858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ochong</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Van den Broek</surname><given-names>IVF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ke